{"url": "https://www.bu.edu/biology", "final_url": "https://www.bu.edu/biology/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Biology\nSkip to Main Content\nArts & Sciences\nBiology\nMenu\nSearch\nPeople\nFaculty\nStudents\nStaff\nAlumni\nBiology Antiracism Committee\nJob Openings\nContact Us\nNews & Events\nEvents Calendar\nFaculty News\nStudent News\nAlumni News\nResearch\nCell & Molecular Biology\nEcology, Behavior & Evolution\nMarine Biology\nNeurobiology\nUndergraduate\nAcademic Advising & Faculty Mentoring\nAcademic Help & Wellness\nAwards & Grants\nBA/MS in Biology\nCareers/Grad School\nCourses\nFAQs\nForms\nMajors\nRegistration\nResearch & Internships\nStudent Groups\nStudy Abroad and Experiential Education\nTransfer Credits and Petitions\nGraduate\nApply to Our Graduate Programs\nBiology Prospective Scholars Program\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD)\nMaster of Science (MS)\nGraduate Research\nAwards & Fellowships\nGraduate Student News\nGraduate Beat (Newsletter)\nGraduate Program Resources\nPostdoc\nPATS Program\nOboh-Weilke Postdoctoral Travel Award\nK-12 Teachers\nResources:\nAdministrative Resources\nApplications and Forms\nHelpful Links\nReservations\nDonate\nSearch\nSearch for:\nBIOLOGY\nAcademics\nWelcome to the Department of Biology\nBiology at Boston University is a highly integrative department, with faculty teaching and conducting research in the broad range of fields that comprise the contemporary life sciences. The department spans the full spectrum of biological sciences, ranging from cell and molecular biology to ecology and conservation biology, giving us unusual strength in integrative research that addresses questions across multiple levels of biological complexity. The Biology Department is committed to providing a safe, inclusive, equitable, and welcoming environment for all.\nAcademics\nLearn More\nFaculty\nLearn More\nResearch\nCell & Molecular Biology\nLearn More\nEcology, Behavior & Evolution\nLearn More\nMarine Biol